{"at":"2026-08-11T22:25:48.880Z","step":"paper","list_items":0,"markers":[],"legend":"STATED\nA source says this directly.\nCONCLUDED\nAxial put sources together. Most likely to be wrong.\nRUNS PAST\nBeyond what the books support. Labelled, not removed.","chars":5522,"head":"My judgment is that Ottoman registration created the Mandate's landholding class in the stronger causal sense: it legally crystallized and enlarged an already emerging class of notables and tax farmers, while the Mandate chiefly consolidated and governed through that class rather than making it from scratch.\n\nRUNS PAST THE BOOKS\nAyubi, Nazih N.; (1995) · T H E O T T O M A N S AND T H E MILITARY/IQ"}
